#
# Semantic checks of the header: values, relations between constants,
# types and macros used at run time. Presence and type shape of every
# name are the Tier 0 header check's. The header mutants for these arrive
# with the Tier 0 generator, so each says why it has no mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.001
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/SEM_FAILED
class      required
since      2001
says       SEM_FAILED has type sem_t *.
test       t/001-sem-failed.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.002
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/sem_t
class      required
says       <semaphore.h> defines the type sem_t.
test       t/002-types-base.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.003
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/timespec
class      required
since      2024
says       <semaphore.h> defines struct timespec as a complete type.
test       t/003-complete-timespec.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.004
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/O_CREAT
class      required
since      2024
says       <semaphore.h> defines the macros O_CREAT, O_EXCL.
test       t/004-macros-open-flags.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.005
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/sem_clockwait
class      required
since      2024
says       <semaphore.h> declares sem_clockwait() with the prototypes
           the page gives.
test       t/005-functions-sem-clockwait.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.semaphore.h.006
anchor     basedefs/semaphore.h.html#DESCRIPTION/sem_close
class      required
says       <semaphore.h> declares sem_close(), sem_destroy(),
           sem_getvalue(), sem_init(), sem_open(), sem_post(),
           sem_timedwait(), sem_trywait(), sem_unlink(), sem_wait() with
           the prototypes the page gives.
test       t/006-functions.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
